(Photosynthesis) Tj T*
(Photosynthesis is the process plants use to turn light energy into chemical energy.) Tj T*
(It takes place in the chloroplasts, which contain the green pigment chlorophyll.) Tj T*
(The light-dependent reactions happen in the thylakoid membranes and produce ATP and NADPH.) Tj T*
(Water is split during these reactions, releasing oxygen as a by-product.) Tj T*
(The Calvin cycle happens in the stroma and uses ATP and NADPH to fix carbon dioxide.) Tj T*
(The overall equation: 6CO2 + 6H2O + light energy -> C6H12O6 + 6O2.) Tj T*
(Glucose made in photosynthesis is used for respiration or stored as starch.) Tj T*
